# Dev Services via Docker Compose

## Hard rule

When starting, restarting, or rebuilding **backend API** and/or **Manage (admin) frontend** for this repo:

1. **Do not** use local `mvn spring-boot:run` / IDE Run for the API as the default path (port `9011` conflicts with Compose).
2. **Do** use the root [`docker-compose.yml`](docker-compose.yml).
3. **Always** run `mvn clean package` (tests skippable) and refresh `senior-post-api/dist/*.jar` **before** rebuilding/recreating `senior-post-api`.

Flutter App remains local (`flutter run`); it is not in Compose.

## Preferred commands (repo root)

PowerShell (Windows):

```powershell
.\scripts\dev-up.ps1
# or API only:
.\scripts\dev-up.ps1 -ApiOnly
```

Manual equivalent:

```powershell
cd senior-post-api
mvn clean package "-Dmaven.test.skip=true"
Copy-Item .\server\target\senior-post-server-*.jar .\dist\ -Force
cd ..
docker compose build senior-post-api
docker compose up -d
```

- API: `http://localhost:9011/backend`
- Manage (Vite in Compose): `http://localhost:8080` (mapped from container `5174`)
- Postgres host port: `65432` (see compose)

## Agent checklist

- [ ] `mvn clean package` completed this start cycle
- [ ] JAR copied into `senior-post-api/dist/`
- [ ] `docker compose build` / `up` used (not bare Spring Boot on host)
- [ ] If `9011` bind fails, stop the conflicting host process or recreate the API container
